the start date for godzilla and king  kong's event has been confirmed plus  we're gonna go over some details for  halo's last spartan standing mode  if you're a fan of giant lizards and  apes well this story is for you  activision has revealed the call of duty  season 3 road map for both vanguard and  warzone which includes the operation  monarch event centered around godzilla  and king kong for those of you  interested in the lore monarch is the  name of the fictional science company  from 2014's godzilla movie season 3 will  arrive on april 27th packed with new  operators weapons a new battle pass and  more operation monarch however begins on  may 11th while the event is still a ways  away activision teased map changes and  secrets to uncover on the island in  preparation for the arrival of the  hollywood titans season 3 will also add  new multiplayer maps as well as a new  gulag location mayhem will be a small  map available at launch while sphere is  another small size map but coming later  in the season another major addition to  multiplayer is the trophy system  equipment coming to vanguard as a new  field upgrade which will allow players  to help avoid death by vanguard's wealth  of lethal and tactical equipment the  vanguard update will go live on april  26th at 9am pacific 12 p.m eastern and  the war zone update will go live on  april 27th at the same time now let's  switch gears and talk about another  shooter that's preparing for a new  season halo infinite today developer 343  industries provided a rundown of some of  the new and returning modes fans can  expect with the new season this includes  the battle royale like last spartan  standing mode which is all about  fighting for survival 12 players spawn  onto big team battle maps with a  confined loadout and 5 respawns run out  of lives and it's all over the players  can still spectate or quit without being  penalized multiplayer designer zack  boyce said in a blog post that an early  version of live spartan standing did not  include set loadouts which led people to  camp and hide banking their respawns and  power weapons in a gun game style twist  players can upgrade a different weapon  with each kill this should sound pretty  familiar to those who know halo's  escalation slayer last barton standing  ends when one spartan remains alive so  this is definitely a battle royale like  mode even if 343 did not use that  terminology last barton standing will be  available in halo infinite when lone  wolves launches on may 3rd and halo  isn't the only game getting a mode with  battle royale influence rocket league is  adding a new limited time event called  knockout bash on april 27th in which  players will battle it out to be the  last car standing unlike rocket league's  regular soccer modes knockout bash  ditches balls and goals as eight players  must knock each other off of platforms  or into hazards until one player remains  this mode will play out across three  different arenas and players will need  to master new gameplay mechanics such as  blocking and grabbing if they want to  survive the free-for-all action knockout  doesn't have unlimited respawns as  players will be knocked out of the game  once they've been eliminated three times  any player knocked into the safe zone  will have 10 seconds to return to the  arena with that arena shrinking in size  knockout bash will be live from april 27  to may 10th honestly out of everything  we just talked about that knockout bash  mode is what's got me the most excited  but let me know in the comments what  you're most excited to try out you can  follow me on twitter at devante chisholm  and i will see you  tomorrow  [Music]
 

